# 必考词 Unit12
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit12核心词汇

{{abbreviation}}{{/əˌbriːviˈeɪʃn}}{{n. 缩写；缩写词}}{{"Dr." is an abbreviation for "Doctor."}}
{{abide}}{{/əˈbaɪd}}{{v. 遵守；忍受；持续；停留}}{{You must abide by the rules of the club.}}
{{abolish}}{{/əˈbɒlɪʃ}}{{v. 废除；取消；彻底消灭}}{{The government decided to abolish the outdated regulation.}}
{{abrupt}}{{/əˈbrʌpt}}{{adj. 突然的；唐突的；陡峭的；粗鲁的}}{{The meeting came to an abrupt end.}}
{{absorb}}{{/əbˈzɔːb}}{{v. 吸收；吸引；理解；承受}}{{Plants absorb carbon dioxide from the atmosphere.}}
{{abstain}}{{/əbˈsteɪn}}{{v. 戒除；弃权；避免；克制}}{{He abstained from voting on the issue.}}
{{absurd}}{{/əbˈsɜːd}}{{adj. 荒谬的；可笑的；不合理的}}{{It is absurd to believe that the earth is flat.}}
{{abundance}}{{/əˈbʌndəns}}{{n. 丰富；充裕；大量；富足}}{{The region has an abundance of natural resources.}}
{{abuse}}{{/əˈbjuːz}}{{v./n. 滥用；虐待；辱骂；恶习}}{{The report revealed the abuse of power by some officials.}}
{{accelerate}}{{/əkˈseləreɪt}}{{v. 加速；促进；催促；增长加快}}{{The government aims to accelerate economic growth.}}
{{accessible}}{{/əkˈsesəbl}}{{adj. 可进入的；易理解的；可获得的；平易近人的}}{{The building is accessible to wheelchair users.}}
{{accommodate}}{{/əˈkɒmədeɪt}}{{v. 容纳；提供住宿；适应；迁就}}{{The hotel can accommodate up to 500 guests.}}
{{accomplish}}{{/əˈkʌmplɪsh}}{{v. 完成；实现；达到；做到}}{{He accomplished his goal of running a marathon.}}
{{accumulate}}{{/əˈkjuːmjəleɪt}}{{v. 积累；积聚；堆积；增加}}{{Dust had accumulated on the shelves over the months.}}
{{accurate}}{{/ˈækjərət}}{{adj. 准确的；精确的；正确的；确切的}}{{The report provides an accurate description of the situation.}}
{{accustom}}{{/əˈkʌstəm}}{{v. 使习惯；使适应；使熟悉}}{{It took her a while to accustom herself to the new environment.}}
{{achieve}}{{/əˈtʃiːv}}{{v. 达到；取得；实现；获得成功}}{{She achieved great success in her scientific research.}}
{{acknowledge}}{{/əkˈnɒlɪdʒ}}{{v. 承认；致谢；确认；注意到}}{{He acknowledged his mistake and apologized publicly.}}
{{acquaint}}{{/əˈkweɪnt}}{{v. 使熟悉；使了解；使认识；通知}}{{Let me acquaint you with the facts of the case.}}
{{acquire}}{{/əˈkwaɪər}}{{v. 获得；学到；收购；养成}}{{She acquired a new skill through online courses.}}
{{activate}}{{/ˈæktɪveɪt}}{{v. 激活；使活动；触发；开动}}{{The alarm was activated by the smoke.}}
{{acute}}{{/əˈkjuːt}}{{adj. 急性的；敏锐的；严重的；剧烈的}}{{The patient has acute appendicitis.}}
{{adapt}}{{/əˈdæpt}}{{v. 适应；改编；调整；改造}}{{It is important to adapt to changing circumstances.}}
{{adequate}}{{/ˈædɪkwət}}{{adj. 足够的；适当的；胜任的；勉强够的}}{{The supply of food is adequate for the refugees.}}
{{adhere}}{{/ədˈhɪər}}{{v. 粘附；坚持；遵守；追随}}{{You must adhere to the safety regulations.}}
{{adjacent}}{{/əˈdʒeɪsnt}}{{adj. 邻近的；毗连的；紧接的；附近的}}{{The hotel is adjacent to the beach.}}
{{adjust}}{{/əˈdʒʌst}}{{v. 调整；适应；校准；调节}}{{You need to adjust the mirror before driving.}}
{{administer}}{{/ədˈmɪnɪstər}}{{v. 管理；执行；给予；实施}}{{The nurse administered the medicine to the patient.}}
{{adolescent}}{{/ˌædəˈlesnt}}{{n./adj. 青少年；青春期的；未成熟的}}{{Adolescent health is an important public health issue.}}
{{adopt}}{{/əˈdɒpt}}{{v. 采用；收养；接受；批准}}{{The company decided to adopt a new strategy.}}
{{adverse}}{{/ˈædvɜːs}}{{adj. 不利的；有害的；相反的；敌对的}}{{The drug has adverse side effects.}}
{{advocate}}{{/ˈædvəkeɪt}}{{v./n. 提倡；倡导者；拥护者；辩护律师}}{{Many scientists advocate for renewable energy sources.}}
{{affiliate}}{{/əˈfɪlieɪt}}{{v./n. 使附属；附属机构；成员；分会}}{{The hospital is affiliated with the university.}}
{{affirm}}{{/əˈfɜːm}}{{v. 断言；肯定；确认；证实}}{{The witness affirmed that the statement was true.}}
{{affluent}}{{/ˈæfluənt}}{{adj. 富裕的；丰富的；富饶的；繁荣的}}{{The affluent neighborhood has many luxury homes.}}
{{aggravate}}{{/ˈæɡrəveɪt}}{{v. 加重；使恶化；激怒；使更糟}}{{The bad weather aggravated his illness.}}
{{aggregate}}{{/ˈæɡrɪɡeɪt}}{{v./n. 聚集；合计；总数；骨料}}{{The aggregate score of the two games was 5-3.}}
{{aggressive}}{{/əˈɡresɪv}}{{adj. 侵略性的；有进取心的；好斗的；积极的}}{{The company adopted an aggressive marketing strategy.}}
{{agitate}}{{/ˈædʒɪteɪt}}{{v. 煽动；使焦虑；搅动；鼓动}}{{The news agitated the public.}}
{{alert}}{{/əˈlɜːt}}{{adj./v./n. 警觉的；提醒；警报；警惕}}{{The government issued an alert about the approaching typhoon.}}
{{alienate}}{{/ˈeɪliəneɪt}}{{v. 使疏远；离间；转让；让渡}}{{His behavior alienated his friends.}}
{{allege}}{{/əˈledʒ}}{{v. 宣称；指控；断言；据说}}{{He is alleged to have committed the crime.}}
{{alleviate}}{{/əˈliːvieɪt}}{{v. 减轻；缓解；缓和；使容易忍受}}{{The medicine helped alleviate the pain.}}
{{allocate}}{{/ˈæləkeɪt}}{{v. 分配；拨出；指定；部署}}{{The government allocated funds for education.}}
{{alternate}}{{/ˈɔːltəneɪt}}{{v./adj. 交替；轮流的；备选的；间隔的}}{{We alternate between working from home and the office.}}
{{alternative}}{{/ɔːlˈtɜːnətɪv}}{{n./adj. 替代品；可选择的；备选的；非传统的}}{{We need to find an alternative solution to this problem.}}
{{ambiguous}}{{/æmˈbɪɡjuəs}}{{adj. 模棱两可的；含糊的；不明确的；引起歧义的}}{{The instructions were ambiguous and confusing.}}
{{amend}}{{/əˈmend}}{{v. 修改；改善；修正；改正}}{{The law was amended to include new provisions.}}
{{analogy}}{{/əˈnælədʒi}}{{n. 类比；类推；相似；类似之处}}{{He drew an analogy between the brain and a computer.}}
{{anchor}}{{/ˈæŋkər}}{{n./v. 锚；使固定；主持人；支柱；依靠}}{{The ship dropped anchor in the harbor.}}
{{annual}}{{/ˈænjuəl}}{{adj. 年度的；每年的；一年一次的；全年的}}{{The annual report shows significant growth in revenue.}}
{{anonymous}}{{/əˈnɒnɪməs}}{{adj. 匿名的；无名的；不知姓名的；不具名的}}{{The donation was made by an anonymous donor.}}
{{anticipate}}{{/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt}}{{v. 预期；期望；预料；预见；先于…做}}{{We anticipate a significant increase in demand.}}
{{apparatus}}{{/ˌæpəˈreɪtəs}}{{n. 器械；设备；机构；器官；体制}}{{The laboratory has modern scientific apparatus.}}
{{apparent}}{{/əˈpærənt}}{{adj. 明显的；表面上的；显而易见的；似乎真实的}}{{It was apparent that she was not telling the truth.}}
{{appeal}}{{/əˈpiːl}}{{v./n. 呼吁；上诉；吸引力；恳求；诉诸}}{{The charity made an appeal for donations.}}
{{appliance}}{{/əˈplaɪəns}}{{n. 器具；家用电器；应用；设备}}{{The kitchen is equipped with modern appliances.}}
{{applicable}}{{/əˈplɪkəbl}}{{adj. 适用的；可应用的；合适的；生效的}}{{The rule is applicable to all employees.}}
{{appoint}}{{/əˈpɔɪnt}}{{v. 任命；指定；约定；确定；下令}}{{He was appointed as the new department manager.}}
{{appraise}}{{/əˈpreɪz}}{{v. 评估；鉴定；评价；估价；鉴定}}{{Experts appraised the value of the painting.}}
{{appreciate}}{{/əˈpriːʃieɪt}}{{v. 感激；欣赏；理解；增值；意识到}}{{I really appreciate your help with this project.}}
{{apprehend}}{{/ˌæprɪˈhend}}{{v. 逮捕；理解；忧虑；领会；认识到}}{{The police apprehended the suspect.}}
{{approach}}{{/əˈprəʊtʃ}}{{v./n. 接近；方法；途径；态度；处理}}{{We need to approach this problem from a different perspective.}}
{{appropriate}}{{/əˈprəʊpriət}}{{adj. 适当的；合适的；恰当的；相称的}}{{Please wear appropriate clothing for the interview.}}
{{approve}}{{/əˈpruːv}}{{v. 批准；赞成；同意；认可；满意}}{{The board approved the new budget plan.}}
{{apt}}{{/æpt}}{{adj. 恰当的；易于…的；聪明的；有…倾向的}}{{She is apt to forget things when she is busy.}}
{{arbitrary}}{{/ˈɑːbɪtrəri}}{{adj. 任意的；武断的；专制的；随机的}}{{The decision seemed arbitrary and unfair.}}
{{arise}}{{/əˈraɪz}}{{v. 出现；产生；起身；起床；源于}}{{New challenges may arise during the project.}}
{{array}}{{/əˈreɪ}}{{n./v. 排列；一系列；部署；大批；阵容}}{{The store has a wide array of products.}}
{{articulate}}{{/ɑːˈtɪkjuleɪt}}{{adj./v. 善于表达的；清楚表达；发音清晰的；明确的}}{{She is very articulate and persuasive in debates.}}
{{ascend}}{{/əˈsend}}{{v. 上升；攀登；登基；追溯；登上}}{{They ascended the mountain slowly.}}
{{ascertain}}{{/ˌæsəˈteɪn}}{{v. 查明；确定；弄清；探知}}{{The police are trying to ascertain the cause of the fire.}}
{{ascribe}}{{/əˈskraɪb}}{{v. 归因于；归咎于；认为…属于；把…归于}}{{He ascribed his success to hard work.}}
{{aspire}}{{/əˈspaɪər}}{{v. 渴望；追求；有志于；向往}}{{She aspires to become a doctor.}}
{{assemble}}{{/əˈsembl}}{{v. 集合；组装；装配；收集；聚集}}{{The students assembled in the auditorium for the lecture.}}
{{assert}}{{/əˈsɜːt}}{{v. 断言；主张；维护；坚持；声称}}{{She asserted her right to speak at the meeting.}}
{{assess}}{{/əˈses}}{{v. 评估；评价；评定；估算；征收}}{{Teachers assess students' progress through regular tests.}}
{{asset}}{{/ˈæset}}{{n. 资产；有价值的人或物；优点；有利条件}}{{Her experience is a valuable asset to the company.}}
{{assign}}{{/əˈsaɪn}}{{v. 分配；指定；指派；布置；转让}}{{The teacher assigned homework to the students.}}
{{assimilate}}{{/əˈsɪmɪleɪt}}{{v. 同化；吸收；消化；理解；融入}}{{Immigrants often assimilate into the local culture.}}
{{assist}}{{/əˈsɪst}}{{v. 帮助；协助；援助；促进；出席}}{{The nurse assisted the doctor during the operation.}}
{{associate}}{{/əˈsəʊʃieɪt}}{{v./n. 联系；同事；伙伴；副的；联想}}{{People often associate the color red with passion.}}
{{assume}}{{/əˈsjuːm}}{{v. 假设；承担；呈现；就职；假装}}{{Let's assume that the project will be completed on time.}}
{{assure}}{{/əˈʃʊər}}{{v. 保证；使确信；确保；向…保证；使放心}}{{I assure you that the product is of high quality.}}
{{attach}}{{/əˈtætʃ}}{{v. 附上；重视；系；贴；使依恋}}{{Please attach your resume to the email.}}
{{attain}}{{/əˈteɪn}}{{v. 达到；获得；实现；到达；赢得}}{{She attained the highest score in the class.}}
{{attempt}}{{/əˈtempt}}{{v./n. 尝试；企图；试图；努力；攻击}}{{He attempted to climb the mountain but failed.}}
{{attend}}{{/əˈtend}}{{v. 出席；照料；注意；处理；伴随}}{{All students are expected to attend the lecture.}}
{{attribute}}{{/əˈtrɪbjuːt}}{{v./n. 归因于；属性；特质；标志；定语}}{{She attributed her success to hard work.}}
{{audit}}{{/ˈɔːdɪt}}{{v./n. 审计；旁听；检查；查账；审计报告}}{{The company's accounts are audited annually.}}
{{augment}}{{/ɔːɡˈment}}{{v. 增加；扩大；增强；补充；提高}}{{The company augmented its workforce to meet demand.}}
{{authentic}}{{/ɔːˈθentɪk}}{{adj. 真正的；真实的；可靠的；正宗的；可信的}}{{The restaurant serves authentic Italian food.}}
{{authorize}}{{/ˈɔːθəraɪz}}{{v. 授权；批准；认可；委托；允许}}{{The manager authorized the purchase of new equipment.}}
{{automate}}{{/ˈɔːtəmeɪt}}{{v. 使自动化；自动操作；机械化}}{{The factory automated its production line.}}
{{autonomy}}{{/ɔːˈtɒnəmi}}{{n. 自治；自主权；自治权；人身自由}}{{The university has a high degree of academic autonomy.}}
{{avail}}{{/əˈveɪl}}{{v./n. 有用；效用；帮助；利益；效验}}{{All their efforts availed them nothing.}}
{{available}}{{/əˈveɪləbl}}{{adj. 可用的；有空的；可获得的；可见到的}}{{The manager is not available at the moment.}}
{{avert}}{{/əˈvɜːt}}{{v. 避免；转移；防止；挡开；避开}}{{Quick action averted a major disaster.}}
{{avid}}{{/ˈævɪd}}{{adj. 热衷的；渴望的；贪婪的；热心的}}{{She is an avid reader of science fiction.}}
{{avoid}}{{/əˈvɔɪd}}{{v. 避免；避开；逃避；预防；使无效}}{{You should avoid eating too much sugar.}}
{{aware}}{{/əˈweər}}{{adj. 意识到的；知道的；有觉悟的；懂世故的}}{{Are you aware of the risks involved in this project?}}
{{awkward}}{{/ˈɔːkwəd}}{{adj. 尴尬的；笨拙的；难使用的；不合适的}}{{There was an awkward silence after his comment.}}
